C('Polymorphic reporting','class A:\n    def unit(self):\n        return "Pa"\nclass B(A):\n    def unit(self):\n        return "K"\nprint([s.unit() for s in [A(), B()]])',"['Pa', 'K']",["['Pa', 'Pa']","['K', 'K']",'Pa K'],'Each call resolves against the actual receiver’s class.')
T('Which relationship best motivates inheritance?', 'A subclass satisfies the base type’s public contract','Two classes happen to use the same variable name','One object merely contains another','Two files use the same editor','Inheritance expresses a substitutable is-a relationship, not just incidental code overlap.')
T('Information hiding primarily asks clients to depend on:', 'A stable public interface','The exact internal attribute layout','Every temporary local variable','Name-mangled field spellings','Internal representation can then change while documented client behavior remains stable.')
T('A single leading underscore on an attribute means:', 'It is conventionally nonpublic','It is inaccessible to Python code','It is automatically immutable','It belongs to the base class only','Python uses naming conventions to signal intended use without enforcing strict privacy.')
T('Double-leading-underscore name mangling mainly helps:', 'Reduce accidental name collisions in subclasses','Encrypt stored data','Prevent every external access','Make values immutable','Mangling changes attribute names to reduce accidental clashes; it is not a security boundary.')
T('An overriding method should preserve:', 'The promises required by callers of the base interface','Only the original source formatting','Only the original variable names','Every internal step exactly','Substitutability depends on compatible observable behavior and contracts.')
T('What does super() support in a simple single-inheritance override?', 'Delegating to the next class implementation','Creating a second independent receiver','Calling every class in the file','Disabling dynamic dispatch everywhere','It allows an override to reuse or extend inherited behavior using the same receiver.')
T('Why validate a setter before assigning the new value?', 'A rejected update can leave valid prior state intact','Assignment must always precede comparison','It makes invalid input impossible to supply','It eliminates all need for tests','Performing checks first prevents partial mutation for the rejected condition.')
T('Which is a risk of returning a mutable internal list directly?', 'Clients can bypass validation by mutating it','Clients can no longer read it','The list becomes automatically immutable','The return statement always copies it','The reference exposes the same storage the object uses internally.')
T('A shallow copy of a list of lists:', 'Copies the outer list but shares the inner objects','Recursively copies every nested value','Creates only a second name for the same outer list','Converts every inner list to a tuple','Shallow copying reproduces one container level; nested mutable objects remain shared.')
T('Which test checks polymorphism meaningfully?', 'Pass different valid implementations through the same client operation','Inspect only one class’s filename','Rename every method before each call','Require exact type equality for all receivers','A common client exercises whether each object honors the required interface.')
T('Which is usually preferable to inheritance for a device containing a logger?', 'Composition','Making Logger a subclass of Device merely for containment','Duplicating every logger method manually','Using an unrelated global list without a contract','Containment is a has-a relationship; composition represents it directly.')
T('If a subclass defines __init__, base initialization:', 'Must be invoked explicitly when needed','Always runs automatically first','Can never be called','Runs twice automatically','The subclass initializer replaces lookup of the inherited initializer unless it delegates.')
T('isinstance(child, Base) can be True when:', 'child is an instance of a subclass of Base','Only when type(child) is exactly Base','Only when child has no attributes','Only before __init__ runs','isinstance recognizes subclass instances as instances of the base type.')
T('Which policy avoids mixing an absolute-pressure model with a signed-reading model?', 'State and enforce each model’s own value contract','Assume every sensor rejects negative readings','Assume every sensor accepts all negatives','Use the same label to hide the difference','Different physical/data meanings can require different valid domains; interfaces must state them.')
T('A property allows:', 'Attribute-style access backed by getter/setter logic','Guaranteed physical privacy','Automatic deep copying of every result','Multiple inheritance without classes','Properties can validate or derive values while preserving an attribute-style interface.')
T('Which change most clearly breaks a documented base contract returning a numeric reading?', 'An override returns an unrelated string on valid input','An override computes the same reading differently','An override adds internal comments','An override uses a different local variable name','Callers relying on numeric behavior cannot substitute an unrelated string result safely.')
T('Which shared class setting is safest as a simple default?', 'An immutable unit string','A mutable history list intended to be independent','A mutable per-instance cache shared accidentally','A list of every object’s private readings without a policy','Immutable defaults avoid accidental shared mutation, though instances may still shadow the binding.')
T('Changing internal storage from a list to another representation should preserve:', 'Documented public behavior','All private attribute names for every client','The original memory addresses','Every timing measurement exactly','Encapsulation permits representation changes when interface promises remain intact.')
T('What is method overriding?', 'A subclass supplies an implementation with an inherited method name','A variable receives a larger numeric value','A caller changes an unrelated local variable','A module imports another module','Method lookup can select the subclass implementation for the same public operation.')
T('Which is a reasonable boundary for introductory inheritance practice?', 'A simple hierarchy with explicit contracts and tests','Arbitrary multiple inheritance without a need','Assuming inheritance automatically validates units','Using private-field spellings as the public API','A small hierarchy supports tracing and reasoning without unnecessary machinery.')
T('A method returns tuple(self._values). What does this protect for a flat numeric history?', 'The caller cannot append into the stored list through that tuple','Every nested object is deeply copied','The caller can never inspect values','All future histories become immutable','A tuple snapshot prevents direct list mutation through the returned container; nested objects require separate consideration.')
T('A subclass strengthens a valid-input precondition unexpectedly. Why is that risky?', 'Previously valid base clients may now fail','It always improves substitutability','It guarantees faster execution','It changes only comments','A substitute should accept the inputs promised by the interface it claims to implement.')
T('When two unrelated types both implement read(), a client using only read() illustrates:', 'Interface-based duck typing','Mandatory shared inheritance','Name mangling','Deep copying','The client relies on the supported operation rather than an exact class identity.')
T('Which state test is especially useful after a setter raises an exception?', 'Verify the original valid state remains as specified','Only print the exception class name','Always force the state to None','Ignore the object afterward','Failure behavior includes whether and how state changes; this must match the documented contract.')
T('Why avoid directly accessing a subclass’s mangled base field in ordinary client code?', 'It couples the client to implementation details','Python syntax forbids every such access','It guarantees encryption','It is always faster than a public method','Using the public interface preserves flexibility and avoids depending on internal mangled names.')
