T('For MATLAB vectors, which operator expresses elementwise multiplication?', '.*','* for every vector shape','**','and','MATLAB distinguishes elementwise .* from matrix multiplication *; translation must preserve the intended operation.')
T('In MATLAB, ordinary array indexing starts at:', '1','0','-1','The last entry','MATLAB uses one-based indexing, unlike Python, C++ vectors and Java arrays.')
T('Which Python operator is exponentiation?', '**','^','^^','exp as an infix operator','Python ** raises a value to a power; ^ has a different bitwise meaning.')
T('In C++17, 7 / 2 with both operands of type int evaluates to:', '3','3.5','4','A compile error','Integer division truncates the quotient toward zero; use an appropriate floating operand for a fractional result.')
T('In Java, -7 / 2 with both operands of type int evaluates to:', '-3','-4','-3.5','4','Java integer division truncates toward zero, which differs from Python floor division for negative quotients.')
T('Which C++ expression obtains floating-point division for integer variables a and nonzero b?', 'static_cast<double>(a) / b','static_cast<double>(a / b)','a / b using int operands only','a % b','Converting before division changes the arithmetic; converting an already truncated quotient is too late.')
T('A Java array of length n has valid ordinary indices:', '0 through n-1','1 through n','0 through n','-1 through n-2','Java arrays are zero-based and reject indices outside the allocated range.')
T('Which MATLAB expression selects the first element of vector a?', 'a(1)','a[0]','a(0)','a{0} for an ordinary numeric vector','Numeric-array indexing uses parentheses and starts at one.')
T('Which MATLAB operator expresses ordinary matrix multiplication?', '*','.* in every case','**','^ for two arbitrary matrices','* computes a matrix product when dimensions are compatible; .* is elementwise.')
T('What must be preserved when porting a numerical algorithm?', 'Contract, units, dimensions, update order and error policy','Only variable names','Only indentation','Only the number of source lines','Equivalent syntax is insufficient if numerical meaning or observable behavior changes.')
T('Why is a Python chained comparison unsafe to translate literally as 0 < x < 10 in C++?', 'C++ evaluates the first comparison to a Boolean before the next comparison','C++ has no comparisons','C++ automatically preserves Python chaining semantics','It always produces a compile error','Use an explicit conjunction of the two intended comparisons in C++.')
T('Which C++/Java scalar Boolean operator corresponds to short-circuit and?', '&&','& in every context','and as a Java keyword','.*','&& evaluates the right operand only if the left operand is true in these scalar Boolean contexts.')
T('What does a semicolon usually do at the end of a MATLAB calculation?', 'Suppresses display of that result','Deletes the variable','Ends the whole program','Converts the result to an integer','The calculation still runs and stores its result; automatic display is suppressed.')
T('MATLAB 1:4 includes:', '1, 2, 3, 4','1, 2, 3 only','0, 1, 2, 3','Only 1 and 4','The colon sequence includes the endpoint when the step reaches it, unlike Python range’s exclusive stop.')
T('Which language feature differs between Python names and typical Java variable declarations?', 'Java variables have declared static types','Python values have no types','Java objects cannot have methods','Python cannot store integers','Python names can be rebound dynamically; Java declaration types constrain assignments at compile time.')
T('A successful compilation demonstrates:', 'Acceptance of the program by that compiler under the supplied options','Correct physical assumptions','Correct output for every input','No runtime exceptions are possible','Compilation checks language/type requirements but does not establish full functional correctness.')
T('Why use shared small fixtures when comparing implementations across languages?', 'They expose semantic differences against independently justified results','They force identical memory layouts','They guarantee identical runtimes','They remove every floating-point difference','Equivalent inputs and expectations reveal translation mistakes in values, units and boundaries.')
T('Which claim about a MATLAB snippet reviewed but not executed is accurate?', 'Its result is derived or reviewed, with native execution unverified','It passed MATLAB runtime tests','A Python analogue proves MATLAB execution succeeded','Compilation and execution are the same','Execution claims must reflect what was actually run; an analogue provides different evidence.')
T('Why check integer division explicitly in a translation?', 'Operand types can change fractional-result behavior','Division has identical semantics in every language','All divisions round down in every language','Changing variable names changes the quotient','The same-looking expression can truncate, floor or perform true division depending on language and types.')
T('What is a dimension check before a matrix product?', 'Verify inner dimensions are compatible','Verify both matrices have the same filename','Verify every value is positive','Verify both arrays have only one row','An m-by-k matrix multiplies a k-by-n matrix to produce an m-by-n result.')
T('A numerical port changes the update order from simultaneous old-state updates to sequential updates. This can:', 'Change the mathematical scheme and results','Only affect comments','Never affect output','Guarantee greater accuracy','Later sequential calculations may use already updated state instead of the intended old values.')
T('Which Python representation requires care because rows may be aliased?', '[[0]*3]*2','[[0]*3 for _ in range(2)]','[1, 2, 3]','tuple([1, 2, 3])','Repetition duplicates references to one row, so modifying a row entry can affect multiple apparent rows.')
T('What should a cross-language error policy specify?', 'How invalid inputs and unavailable results are reported','Only a preferred editor','Only the source-file extension','That every exception is ignored','Different languages have different mechanisms; the interface meaning should remain explicit.')
T('Which is a transferable idea across Python, MATLAB, C++ and Java?', 'Decomposition into clear operations with tested contracts','Identical array syntax','Identical integer division','Identical memory ownership rules','Problem structure and validation principles transfer even when syntax and runtime semantics differ.')
T('A correct numerical result in another language should be compared using:', 'A justified exact or tolerance-based criterion appropriate to the result','String equality of every diagnostic line only','Any tolerance large enough to pass','The same number of source lines','Comparison should preserve relevant numeric meaning and account for legitimate representation differences.')
