T('An engineering computation should begin by stating:', 'Inputs, outputs, units, assumptions and valid domains','Only the plotting color','Only a function name','Only a desired runtime','A clear problem contract supports correct implementation and meaningful interpretation.')
T('Why keep raw measurements separate from processed values?', 'To preserve evidence and make transformations traceable','To guarantee sensors never fail','To avoid documenting conversions','To prevent all data analysis','Separate raw data allow checking, revising and reproducing processing choices.')
T('A report omits rejected records. What else should it communicate?', 'The rejection policy and enough counts/context to interpret the result','That no records were rejected','Only the final rounded mean','An unrelated benchmark','Filtering can change conclusions; readers need to understand the retained dataset and exclusions.')
T('Which preserves timestamp meaning after filtering missing readings?', 'Keep each retained reading paired with its original timestamp','Renumber all timestamps without disclosure','Replace every missing reading by zero automatically','Sort readings independently of times','Values and times form related records and must remain aligned.')
T('A mean is undefined for an empty retained dataset. The implementation should:', 'Use an explicit documented empty-result policy','Divide by zero deliberately','Return an arbitrary plausible mean','Reuse a stale previous mean silently','Empty-input handling is part of the computation contract.')
T('What distinguishes numerical error from model error?', 'Numerical error concerns the computation; model error concerns how assumptions represent reality','They are always identical','Only model error can affect results','A passing unit test eliminates both','Correct code can implement an inadequate model, and a suitable model can be computed inaccurately.')
T('Why test boundary values in an alarm or classification rule?', 'Equality and nearby values can select different branches','Only large values can expose bugs','Boundaries never occur in real data','Averages automatically test every boundary','Tests around thresholds reveal off-by-one and inequality-policy errors.')
T('Which is a sound check for a sorting routine?', 'Compare ordered output and full element multiplicities with the input','Check only that the output sum is unchanged','Check only the first item','Check only that the program did not raise','Aggregate sums alone can match despite missing or altered entries; multiplicity preservation matters.')
T('A graph has no unit labels. What is missing?', 'Information needed to interpret the numerical axes','Proof of faster runtime','A guarantee of sorting stability','A recursion base case','Axes need meaningful quantities and units so readers can interpret scale and relationships.')
T('Which function decomposition is useful for a measurement report?', 'Separate parsing, validation, calculation and presentation','Put every task in one broad silent exception handler','Mix rounding into every internal update','Use global state for every intermediate value','Separating concerns makes individual contracts easier to test and revise.')
T('Why retain full precision internally and round for display when appropriate?', 'Repeated early rounding can accumulate error or change decisions','Formatted text is always more accurate than numbers','Rounding removes all measurement uncertainty','Every algorithm requires integer output','Presentation precision and computational precision serve different purposes.')
T('A bisection root algorithm requires an initial bracket under its usual continuity contract. Which check is relevant?', 'Endpoint signs enclose a sign change, with exact roots handled deliberately','The endpoints have the same printed width','The lower endpoint must equal zero','The midpoint must already be the root','Continuity plus an appropriate sign bracket supports retaining a root-containing interval.')
T('Why include both an error criterion and an iteration limit in an approximation routine?', 'To define convergence and a bounded failure path','To guarantee every model is physically correct','To force the same number of iterations for all inputs','To eliminate floating-point arithmetic','A limit prevents unbounded work when the desired criterion is not reached.')
T('What is the correct basis for optimizing a slow workflow?', 'Identify the relevant costly work while preserving the contract','Always rewrite it in another language first','Remove required outputs first','Compare source line counts only','Measure or count the actual bottleneck and verify an equivalent result after changes.')
T('A cached result can be reused safely only when:', 'The cache key captures all inputs/state affecting that result','The function name is unchanged','The last result looks plausible','The output is numeric','Missing dependencies can return stale results even when lookup is fast.')
T('What does a successful finite regression suite provide?', 'Evidence for the tested cases and conditions','Proof of correctness for every possible input','Proof of physical safety','A guarantee of optimal complexity','Tests support a bounded claim and complement reasoning about contracts and invariants.')
T('Which review activity best reveals understanding of code?', 'Predict state and output, explain each step, then run and compare','Copy output without tracing','Memorize only variable names','Read only the final print statement','Prediction and explanation expose the reasoning that execution can then check.')
T('When translating a loop to another language, check:', 'Index origin, endpoint inclusion, types and update order','Only comment punctuation','Only font size','Only filename capitalization','These semantic differences can change iteration counts and numerical results despite similar syntax.')
T('Which is a valid reason to use a class?', 'Related persistent state and operations benefit from one interface','Every mathematical expression needs an object hierarchy','A class guarantees all data are valid automatically','Classes eliminate all test design','Object design is useful when it clarifies state ownership and supported behavior.')
T('What should an inherited interface promise remain across implementations?', 'Compatible valid inputs, results and failure/state behavior','The same private variable names','The same source line count','The same object memory address','Clients depend on observable contracts rather than internal implementation details.')
T('A numerical optimization changes rounding order. What should review include?', 'Accuracy and stability checks as well as speed','Only the fastest timing','Only code length','Assume fewer operations always means more accurate','Arithmetic rearrangement can change finite-precision behavior; performance and accuracy must both be assessed.')
T('What makes a computational result reproducible?', 'Recorded data provenance, processing steps, parameters and relevant environment','Only a screenshot of a final number','Only the author’s name','A claim that defaults were used','Others need enough information to reconstruct the calculation and its conditions.')
T('Which distinguishes required output storage from auxiliary storage?', 'Output holds the promised results; auxiliary storage supports their construction','Both must always be excluded from every memory claim','Output is always constant size','Auxiliary memory means input files only','State explicitly whether a memory bound includes input and output to avoid ambiguity.')
T('How should an unexpected test failure during final review be treated?', 'Investigate the first divergence against the intended contract','Suppress the test to make the summary green','Change the answer key immediately without justification','Assume the machine is wrong','The failure can expose implementation, fixture or expectation mistakes and deserves diagnosis.')
T('What is the purpose of these Week 14 practice questions?', 'Formative review integrating the course concepts','A declaration of the final examination contents','A new grading policy','A substitute for current course announcements','Practice supports learning; it does not announce assessment format, rules or obligations.')
